.TH TEATHER-GTK 1 "September 2026" "Teather 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
teather-gtk \- graphical Teather Linux USB desktop client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B teather-gtk
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B teather-gtk
opens the focused GTK 3 interface for device approval and selection, connection
state, counters, diagnostics, auto-connect, and remembered-device management.
Its controls are grouped into labelled sections (Connection, This phone,
Preferences, Activity); connection state is shown as a coloured status pill, and
byte counters use human-readable units. Session history, Diagnostics, and a
window restart live in the HeaderBar menu; Session history opens a table of
recent connections (duration and bytes each way) read from the daemon. It also offers an
Appearance setting (follow system / light / dark, stored in
.IR ~/.config/teather/gui.json )
and a button that installs or updates the phone app from the copy this package
bundles. When Ayatana AppIndicator is available it also provides a tray menu;
the main window remains functional without tray integration. Launching
.B teather-gtk
again takes over any running window rather than re-presenting it, so a window
left open across a package upgrade is replaced by one running the new code.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR teather (1),
.BR teatherd (1)
